# full - a Wayland system: every package the build produces which belongs on a
# running system, less the X server and the desktop it carried, in build order.
#
# It used to be every runtime package without exception, and the generator
# below still produces that. What is subtracted from it now is a choice rather
# than a rule: the X server, the session that started it, and Firefox. This
# distro runs cog on DRM instead - the browser draws straight to KMS with no
# compositor and no X server between it and the screen.
#
# The X client libraries stay, and that is not an oversight. mesa is built
# '-Dplatforms=x11,wayland', so libEGL links libxcb and libX11 whether or not
# anything ever opens a display. Dropping them means a second mesa built for
# Wayland alone, which is a bigger change than this one and buys a few
# megabytes.
#
# Generated, minus distros/core/packages.list, minus the packages whose build
# script carries a '# BUILD_ONLY:' line, minus the X server and Firefox set
# listed in distros/full/packages.drop. Regenerate after adding a package:
#
#   ./scripts/packages/list-runtime-packages.sh \
#     | grep -vxF -f <(grep -vE '^\s*#|^\s*$' distros/core/packages.list) \
#     | grep -vxF -f <(grep -vE '^\s*#|^\s*$' distros/full/packages.drop)

